{"author":{"id":"6af04b5756f10b3005a23338b8f25a6c1d7564fe1ddddc77e70806b2f14ac31a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788929796,"nonce":"BWcn423JuHDqgb9vdEwbikKJd6A=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABQZOMpw","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/gic-lang/issues/9","origin":"github"},"title":"Support documentation comments in GIC","message":"Add JSDoc-style documentation comments for GIC declarations so user-defined functions, parameters, variables, and reusable library code can explain their purpose and appear in IDE hover or completion information.\n\nThis should be a small GIC-specific documentation format rather than full JavaScript JSDoc compatibility. The language currently supports only // line comments, so the design must decide whether documentation uses consecutive /// comments, /** ... */ blocks, or another minimal syntax.\n\nBefore implementation, specify:\n- which declarations can receive documentation\n- whether parameter and return descriptions are supported\n- how documentation is represented in the AST or analyzer metadata\n- how ordinary comments differ from documentation comments\n- how the planned browser IDE exposes the documentation\n\nSuccess criteria:\n- documented syntax is added to the language specification\n- lexer and parser preserve documentation comments where required\n- malformed documentation produces clear behavior\n- tests cover declaration association\n- IDE hover can display preserved documentation","files":null}]}